# ⛔ 6.7.14 (the user's D7 (a), 2026-10-16) — EXPLICIT TYPE ARGUMENTS ON A METHOD CALL, as on its free spelling:
# `p.id<f64>(h)`, `w.v.id<f64>(h)`, `var a = p.id<f64>(h);` call `P_id$f64`, as `P_id<f64>(&p, h)` does. The `<`
