# ⛔ 6.7.13 — AN INLINE `Str` IS ITS HEADER'S ADDRESS WHERE A `Str` VALUE IS TAKEN (the user's decision D7 (1),
# 2026-10-15). A `Str` is a heap handle by name — its slot holds a 16 B header's address — but `var t: Str = Str {
# p, 7 };` (or, since 6.7.14, a bare `var t: Str;` — D20 (a)) is an INLINE header whose slot is field 0, so `f(t)`
# into `s: Str`, `str_len(t)`, `var
