# is a handle global (8 bytes) holding it — `H.len = 3` writes gt.len — in the declaration zone and after the first
# statement alike. Both made H an inline 16-byte COPY of gt (`_gci_inline` / `_gci_init`, `_gci_toplevel`). A `var P:
# *Str = gt;` in the zone takes the same address, as after the first statement (6.7.14's D18 (c)). The untyped `var
