# `= callptr(&mk3, 5);` — the callee written `&f`, so the call carries mk3's struct result (6.7.11, ARG-1) — into an
# annotation that names no struct read P3's first field (n = 5) where `var n: i64 = mk3(5);` is refused (D24). Now
# refused with D24's words, naming mk3, at its name: in a fn, a declaration of no struct type (`pscale` 0, the
# cursor on its initialiser) whose initialiser is one whole such call, inside any parentheses up to its `;`
# (`_rcv_scalar_ann` judges the struct's size, a `Str`, the annotation). The initialiser's first token is marked
