# ⛔ 6.7.10 (B7-1g) — THE HANDLE LINE FOR GLOBALS (the user's decision 5, 2026-10-12: one rule for locals
# and globals at every size). A struct global of 8 B or less initialised from anything that is not a
# struct value of its type is a HANDLE (GVPM 1: its slot holds the address and `G.v = 5` writes the
# object), as one over 8 B always was; a literal or a struct value keeps the inline value slot (GVPM 2).
# Through 6.7.9 every such global was a value whatever its initialiser, so `var G: S8 = alloc(8);` held
# the ADDRESS as `G.v` and its writes stayed in the global. A global declared after the first top-level
# statement (PARSE_VAR) has its initialiser parsed before it is registered, and is judged as a local is
# (`_gz_late`). In the declaration zone (PARSE_GVAR_REG) the initialiser is parsed only by the replay,
# after every fn body, and a call in it may name a fn declared below: the global is registered inline
# and judged once pass 1 has registered every fn (`_gz_sweep`, the end of `_prescan_tail`), from its
# tokens (`_gz_sval`), before any fn body reads its layout. The replay, which parses the initialiser,
# checks that answer against what the parse recorded (`_gz_agree`) and refuses a disagreement by name.
# Every consumer takes a small handle global's struct as it takes a small handle local's (`_hl_gbare`,
# `_ret_small_gh`, `_agc_handle_global`); a handle as an operator's left operand is pointer arithmetic,
# as over 8 B. CHANGELOG [6.7.10]
var _gz_v = 0;   # the declaration zone's struct globals of 8 B or less: (slot, initialiser token) pairs
# `_gz_ty`'s kind of value: 1 a call / method / operator / if-expression result, 2 an inline global, 3 a
# handle global, 4 (retired in 6.7.11: `-g` is an integer), 5 a struct-typed field (a
# struct value; 6.7.10: an operator's left operand dispatches on it, decision 11), 6 a `*T` (the struct it
# points at; a receiver, never a value), 7 a dereference `*E` of a `*T` (6.7.10: an operator's left
# operand dispatches on it; a declaration from it is `_gz_star`'s).
var _gz_k = 0;
var _gz_gb = 0;  # the generic struct a whole generic call's `: G<T>` return names (its instance is the call's)
var _gz_mfi = 0 - 1;   # 6.7.15: the method or operator fn whose result `_gz_ty` last typed (`_gu_wsid`)
# 6.7.16: that step's method name token (-1: an operator fn), its `(` and its receiver's struct (`_gu_minst`)
var _gz_mti = 0 - 1;
var _gz_mop = 0;
var _gz_mrs = 0;
var _gz_mx = 0;        # 6.7.16: 1 while `_gz_ty` splits — `_gz_split` then reads `R.m<..>(` as one operand
# PARSE_GVAR_REG, the slot known (`gvi`; `ti` the initialiser's first token): a struct global of 8 B or
# less is noted for the sweep — a literal (`lit` 1, struct `ssid`) as a fixed value (its token negated),
# any other initialiser (the declared `asid`) to be judged.
fn _gz_reg(S, gvi, lit, ssid, asid, ti): i64 {
